  "source": "Schneider Electric, PowerLogic EM3502, EM3550 Compact Power and Energy Meter Installation Guide ZL0092-0A (11/2011), Modbus Point Map (EM3550 only)",
  "notes": [
    "Modbus RTU on the RS-485 port, functions 03 and 04 (read), 06 and 16 (write). Factory defaults: station address 1, 19200 baud, even parity.",
    "The manual gives one-based register numbers (integer registers start at 001, floating-point registers at 257, configuration at 129); they are written here minus 1, address base 0. Integer and floating-point registers are mirror views of the same measurements; the floating-point ones need no scaling.",
    "The point map is for the EM3550 only; the EM3502 has pulse and alarm outputs but no Modbus port, so it is listed as a model of the family only.",
    "16-bit and 32-bit integer values are scaled by the scale factor registers 138 to 141 (value = raw x 10^exponent, as the manual states); the power factors and frequency use a fixed 0.0001 and 0.01. 32-bit integers and floats carry the most significant register first (high word first); each byte is big-endian.",
    "Values not supported in the selected system type read 0x8000 (integers) or 0x7FC00000 (floats). Reserved registers (25, 136, 148, 151, 154, 305/306) are left out.",
    "The manual describes registers 257/258 and 259/260 identically as real energy consumption, and gives no text for 339/340; they are kept under neutral names. Writes to configuration registers are protected by a user passcode in the meter.",
    "Written from the manufacturer's manual; not tested on a device."
  ],
  "byte_order": "big",
  "word_order": "big",
  "address_base": 0,
  "x_status": "official",
